  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "A Particle System emits small images, called particles, from a shape. The Shape module sets where they are born: a cone, a box, a sphere or a mesh. The Emission module sets how many. Rate over Time gives a steady flow per second; a Burst emits a group at once, at a set time.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> Both emitters release 20 particles each second. The left one uses Rate over Time 20; the right one uses a Burst of 20 every second. How do they look different?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Select the left emitter. In Shape, change Shape from Cone to Box, then to Sphere.\n2. On the right emitter, set the Burst's Count to 100 and its Interval to 3.\n3. Press Restart in the Particles overlay of the Scene view.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Particle-Effects, 3 \xB7 Steam (Rate over Time) and 7 \xB7 Sparks (Bursts)</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
