      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "The particle's material decides how it is drawn. Particles Unlit ignores the lights; Particles Lit and Simple Lit take the colour of the lights around them. Alpha blending covers what is behind, like smoke or dust. Additive blending adds light to it: it can only make the image brighter, like sparks or a glow.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> A red light shines on all four emitters. Which of them turn red?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Switch the red light off and on, and watch which emitters change.\n2. Move the two Additive emitters in front of the white panel, then the black one.\n3. Change one emitter's material from Particles/Unlit to Particles/Lit.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Particle-Effects, 7 \xB7 Sparks (Additive) and 3 \xB7 Steam (Alpha, lit)</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
