  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "By default, particles pass through everything. The Collision module makes them hit the scene's colliders (World) or a few planes (Planes), and then bounce, slow down or die. The Sub Emitters module starts another Particle System at a particle's birth, collision or death: a drop that lands starts a splash.\n\n<b>Predict:</b> Half of this rain falls on a small roof. With Collision on, where do the splashes appear, and what is under the roof?\n\n<b>Try:</b>\n1. Untick Collision and watch the drops.\n2. Tick it again. Set Bounce to 0.5 and Lifetime Loss to 0.\n3. In Sub Emitters, change Collision to Death.\n\n<size=85%><color=#A8A8A8>Reference: Particle-Effects, 1 \xB7 Rain (splash at death) and 2 \xB7 Drips (splash at collision)</color></size>"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 2f7116f10747a67409388e93052ae222, type: 2}
